Subject: [PATCH] bore: adapt the slice-protection bypass to preempt_wakeup_action

CachyOS's 6.18 BORE patch does not build against 6.18.36 and later.

Linux 6.18.36 reworked check_preempt_wakeup_fair(): the local `bool
do_preempt_short` was replaced by `enum preempt_wakeup_action
preempt_action`, with PREEMPT_WAKEUP_SHORT standing in for what
do_preempt_short used to mean ("ignore current's slice protection").

Both copies of the BORE patch in cachyos/kernel-patches still target the
older shape, in different ways:

  * 6.18/sched/0001-bore-cachy.patch     -- fails to apply (one hunk in
    check_preempt_wakeup_fair() is rejected).
  * 6.18/sched-dev/0001-bore-cachy.patch -- applies cleanly but does not
    compile: its hunk assigns to do_preempt_short, which no longer exists.
        kernel/sched/fair.c: In function 'check_preempt_wakeup_fair':
        kernel/sched/fair.c:9010:17: error: 'do_preempt_short' undeclared

This adapts the sched-dev hunk. The BORE block's own comment describes it
as the companion to the in-tree PREEMPT_SHORT path, so it is moved to sit
directly after that check and given the same treatment it now has:

        preempt_action = PREEMPT_WAKEUP_SHORT;
        goto pick;

which is exactly what `do_preempt_short = true` used to produce -- at
`pick:` the flag selects pick_next_entity()'s non-protecting variant, and
at `preempt:` it triggers cancel_protect_slice(). Moving the call also
means do_preempt_weight() now runs after `cfs_rq = cfs_rq_of(se)` and
update_curr(), so entity_eligible() is evaluated against the same, updated
cfs_rq the surrounding checks use, rather than task_cfs_rq(donor).

Apply after 0001-bore-cachy.patch (sched-dev). Drop this file once
upstream refreshes the 6.18 BORE patch for the new enum.
---
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -9000,16 +9000,6 @@
 	if (unlikely(se == pse))
 		return;
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
-	/*
-	 * Likewise, if @p is heavier than current (under BORE: more
-	 * interactive), per kernel.sched_burst_protect_slice_lv, override
-	 * current's slice protection to allow preemption.
-	 */
-	if (do_preempt_weight(cfs_rq, pse, se))
-		do_preempt_short = true;
-#endif
-
 	/*
 	 * This is possible from callers such as attach_tasks(), in which we
 	 * unconditionally wakeup_preempt() after an enqueue (which may have
@@ -9074,6 +9064,18 @@
 		goto pick;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
+	/*
+	 * Likewise, if @p is heavier than current (under BORE: more
+	 * interactive), per kernel.sched_burst_protect_slice_lv, override
+	 * current's slice protection to allow preemption.
+	 */
+	if (do_preempt_weight(cfs_rq, pse, se)) {
+		preempt_action = PREEMPT_WAKEUP_SHORT;
+		goto pick;
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
+
 	/*
 	 * Ignore wakee preemption on WF_FORK as it is less likely that
 	 * there is shared data as exec often follow fork. Do not
